From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phil Reif <pr@sambal.net>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:45:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(frontend): hide deleted threads without replies

A deleted thread root stays as a tombstone while it shows replies. Two cases
kept such rows after all replies were deleted too:

- The room timeline holds no thread replies, so a retracted reply never
  lowered the root's reply count. The tombstone stayed with its old count
  until a reload. After a retraction, the room store now reads the reply
  count of its loaded deleted roots again from the room page around them;
  message reads omit deleted messages. Retractions in quick succession share
  one read.
- The Threads page listed followed threads whose root is deleted and that
  have no replies left, as "Message deleted". The page now omits them.
